      "text": "THE LEIBEL LAB we love the lung RESEARCH Our team studies lung development using cutting-edge in-vitro techniques. Our stem cell-derived 3D human lung organoid models allow us to study various diseases that occur across the human lifespan. Scroll below to see some of the projects our lab is working on! Investigating neonatal respiratory diseases such as nRDS and RSV infection Learn More Studying SARS-CoV-2 infection with stem cell-derived lung organoids and macrophages Learn More Deriving whole, proximal, and distal stem cell-derived human 3D lung organoids Learn More Understanding the protecting factors of breast milk for the neonatal lung Learn More Contact us Israni Biomedical Research Facility Email: saleibel@health.ucsd.edu 7835 Trade St Ste 100 San Diego CA 92121",
